(Declaring a list of the same name as a list parameter names a new list of
 the function's own. Declared in only one branch, the new list lasts as long
 as its condition; after it, the name is the parameter again, the caller's
 list, on both calls.)
To 'maybe replace' with a list called items and a number called choice.
    If choice is 1 then, a list called items is ["local"].
    append "x" to items.
    Print "inside: {items}".

a list called xs is ["old"].
'maybe replace' of xs and 0.
Print "xs: {xs}".
'maybe replace' of xs and 1.
Print "xs: {xs}".
